.TITLE "cp"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Copies files and directories from one location to another. It is used to create __backups__ or move data across the __filesystem__.

.DIV "TLDR"
**cp source destination**
Copies a specific file to a new location or with a new name.
> __source__ the original file | __destination__ the target path

**cp -r folder destination**
Copies an entire directory and all of its contents recursively.
> __-r__ recursive flag | __folder__ source directory | __destination__ target path

**cp -i source destination**
Prompts for confirmation before overwriting an existing file.
> __-i__ interactive flag | __source__ the original file | __destination__ target path

**cp -p source destination**
Preserves the original file attributes such as permissions and timestamps.
> __-p__ preserve flag | __source__ original file | __destination__ target path

**cp -u source destination**
Only copies the file if the source is newer than the destination.
> __-u__ update flag | __source__ original file | __destination__ target path

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using the __-p__ flag is a best practice when creating backups to ensure metadata is kept intact. For large transfers, the __-v__ flag helps you monitor the progress of the copy operation.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:mv** **linux:rm** **linux:rsync**

